  "answer_text": "**ProFed Credit Union** (officially **ProFed Federal Credit Union**) is a community-chartered, member-owned financial institution headquartered in **Fort Wayne, Indiana**. \n\nBelow is a quick overview of what they offer, how to qualify for membership, and key contact details:\n\n### 1. Membership Eligibility\nAs a community-chartered credit union, ProFed is open to anyone who lives, works, worships, volunteers, or regularly conducts business in any of the following nine northeast Indiana counties:\n*   Adams, Allen, DeKalb, Huntington, LaGrange, Noble, Steuben, Wells, and Whitley.\n\n### 2. Services Offered\nProFed offers a full range of personal and business banking products, including:\n*   **Personal Banking:** Checking & savings accounts, student accounts, and digital banking tools.\n*   **Loans:** Mortgages, auto loans, credit cards, and personal loans.\n*   **Business Banking:** Commercial savings & checking, business loans, and employer-sponsored Health Savings Accounts (HSAs).\n*   **Digital Tools:** 24/7 online banking and the ProFed Digital Banking mobile app.\n\n### 3. Key Account & Contact Information\n*   **Routing / Transit Number:** `274973183` (used for direct deposits, ACH transfers, and domestic wire transfers).\n*   **Contact Center:** 260-373-1633 or 800-752-4613 (Ext. 1633)\n*   **Main Office Address:** 1710 St. Joe River Drive, Fort Wayne, IN 46805\n\nYou can access your online banking portal, find nearby branches/ATMs, or apply for membership directly on the [ProFed Credit Union Website](https://www.profedcreditunion.com).",
